<title>SINGAPORE: General Magnetics net loss soars 248 pct.</title>
<headline>General Magnetics net loss soars 248 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net loss				  3.66   vs   1.05</p>
<p>    Group loss per share (cents)	3.70   vs   1.10</p>
<p>    Turnover				 46.87   vs  55.43</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest	 0.08   vs   0.08</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		    0.75   vs   1.29</p>
<p>    Depreciation/amortisation	  10.82   vs   9.80</p>
<p>    Losses from associates		0.29   vs   0.18</p>
<p>    Pre-tax loss			    5.21   vs   2.90</p>
<p>    Tax					 1.96   vs   2.24</p>
<p>    Minorities (losses)		   0.12   vs   0.21</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries (losses)	    9.47   vs   nil</p>
<p>Note - General Magnetics Ltd manufactures magnetic media and related products. It said the closure of loss-making manufacturing operations in Thailand and Singapore accounted for most of the company's extraordinary losses.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
